---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro'
import { site } from '../config/site'
import '../styles/doc.css'
---

<!-- Store-review and ad-network facing page. Keep it plain-language and keep
     it true to Terms Section 6 and Privacy Section 11 (Children). -->
<LegalLayout
  title={`Responsible Play — ${site.name}`}
  description={`${site.name} is a social game played with virtual currency: no real-money stakes, no prizes, no cash-out. How we keep it that way, and how to control spending and playtime.`}
  canonical={`${site.url}/responsible-play`}
>
  <h1>Responsible Play</h1>
  <p class="doc-meta">
    {site.name} is a game, not a betting product. This page says plainly what
    that means for your money, your time, and your family.
  </p>

  <h2>No gambling, in either direction</h2>
  <p>{site.disclaimer}</p>
  <ul>
    <li>You never stake real money on a match.</li>
    <li>You never win real money, goods, or anything redeemable outside the
      app.</li>
    <li>Coins and Gems cannot be sold, traded outside the app, or converted to
      cash.</li>
    <li>A balance of zero is never a loss of money — free Coins come back
      through the hourly bonus, daily missions, and rewards.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The full legal wording is in our <a href="/terms">Terms</a>, Section 6.
  </p>

  <h2>{site.minimumAge}+ only</h2>
  <p>
    The app is for adults aged {site.minimumAge} and over. We do not knowingly
    hold data from children. If you believe a child is using an account, write
    to <a href={`mailto:${site.privacyEmail}`}>{site.privacyEmail}</a> and we
    will remove it.
  </p>

  <h2>Controlling what you spend</h2>
  <p>
    Optional purchases exist and they are all handled by the App Store or
    Google Play, which means the controls you already trust apply:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>iPhone and iPad</strong> — Settings &rsaquo; Screen Time &rsaquo;
      Content &amp; Privacy Restrictions &rsaquo; iTunes &amp; App Store
      Purchases, to require a password or block in-app purchases entirely.</li>
    <li><strong>Android</strong> — Google Play &rsaquo; Settings &rsaquo;
      Authentication &rsaquo; Require authentication for purchases, and Family
      settings for a shared device.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You never have to buy anything. Every board, tier, and reward in the game
    is reachable by playing.
  </p>

  <h2>Keeping it fun</h2>
  <p>Some honest advice from people who play a lot of backgammon:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Play for the match, not to win back a bad session. Variance in
      backgammon is large and short runs prove nothing.</li>
    <li>If you find yourself playing to chase a balance rather than because you
      want a game, stop for the day. Nothing in the app expires.</li>
    <li>Use your phone's own screen-time limits if sessions run longer than you
      intended.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>If gambling is a problem for you</h2>
  <p>
    {site.name} involves no real-money betting, but games with dice and chips
    can still be uncomfortable for someone in recovery. If that is you, the
    honest advice is to skip this app. For help, contact a national gambling
    support service in your country — many run free, confidential helplines and
    chat services.
  </p>

  <h2>Taking a break, or leaving</h2>
  <p>
    You can uninstall at any time and your account waits for you. If you want
    it gone for good, <a href="/delete-account">Delete Your Account</a> explains
    how, and deletion is permanent.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
